{title: What I'm Called to Be}
{artist: Daniel Sullivan}
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 102}

Verse 1
Who am I to be called
a precious son of God
And what have I ever done
to share a place with God's Son

Verse 2
For you saved me from the fall
and have for me a higher call
A higher walk a higher life
To be a member of Christ

Chorus
So I submit to you
help me to see what I am
who I am and what I'm called to be
'cause Lord I need you
help me to be what I am
who I am and what I'm called to be

Verse 3
So put me on the front line
put me there in your time
I'd be glad washing feet
and I'd be glad planting seeds

Verse 4
For this life is not my own
and this ol' world is not my home
I could run and I could fly
but to walk with you, there's my prize

Chorus
So I submit to you
help me to see what I am
who I am and what I'm called to be
'cause Lord I need you
help me to be what I am
who I am and what I'm called to be
